    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Covered is not reachable — and `check:tools` cannot tell you which",
      "prov:value": "Found three times in one session, 2026-09-20, working bean `d308`:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean d308",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two questions, kept apart",
      "prov:value": "> **\"Does this skill have a Tool?\"** — `bun run cat check:tools`, and\n> `bun run cat tools:coverage` for which of the uncovered ones warrant one.\n>\n> **\"Is this command reachable by asking the graph?\"** — nothing yet. Bean\n> `d308` measured it by hand: of 868 code files, 229 are reachable from no node,\n> collapsing to 13 groups."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two reasons NOT to write `maintains`, both judgements rather than omissions",
      "prov:value": "**A `maintains` claim asserts the artefact is published.** Verify that by reading\nthe build, not by assuming. `cat-harness/ns.jsonld` is a real claim because\n`.github/workflows/docs-site.yml` writes it, and that was checked before the claim\nwas made. (The example was `ns/vocabulary.jsonld` until 2026-09-30, when that\nall-layers union was retired and its claim removed in the same change — a\nclaim outliving its artefact is the same 404 from the other side.) An artefact nobody publishes is exactly the 404 the drift check exists\nto prevent.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "And the drift check only covers its own producer",
      "prov:value": "`kg:schema:check` reconciles `maintains` both ways, but its `unproduced`\ndirection runs **only over artefacts whose declaring Tool invokes\n`bun run cat kg:schema`**. It was narrowed on 2026-09-20 because it had encoded a\npremise `maintains` never carried — that a maintained artefact is produced by the\nschema exporter — and reported the first counterexample as drift.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "And the drift check only covers its own producer",
      "prov:value": "So **a `maintains` claim on any other producer's artefact is unchecked.** It can\nrot to a 404 and nothing notices. Bean `6f1x` carries the fix: assert every\ndeclared artefact is present after `_site/` is assembled, with\ncould-not-determine kept distinct from present.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 6f1x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The third case: a mechanism with no skill at all",
      "prov:value": "**Case 5 is case 4's inverse** — the entry point is present and the callers are\nabsent — and it is discussed under [§Reachability is PLURAL](#reachability-is-plural--which-caller-should-this-have-presumes-one)\nbelow, because the useful question there is not *what is missing* but *how many\ndispatch points this should have*. Worked example: `translation-roundtrip.ts`,\nbean `vo9d`, which was **born** callerless in commit `4997840` — its only\nreferences at birth were its own usage string and a line of skill prose telling a\nhuman what to type. That is this skill's own \"mechanism inlined in prose\"\nfailure, and the bean's standing hypothesis — that a caller was *lost* when the\ntranslation simulation was removed — is **struck**: `simulate-translation.ts` had\nits own private `roundTripQA()` over a hand-written map and never called the\nscript. A path cannot lose a caller it never had.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean vo9d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The third case: a mechanism with no skill at all",
      "prov:value": "Case 3 was met on 2026-09-20: `gen-themes-css` and `gen-avatars-css` render theme\nand avatar nodes into `assets/css/themes.css` and `assets/css/avatars.css`. Both\nare committed, published, single-file artefacts — a textbook `maintains` pair. And\n**no skill in the corpus states the capability.** `kg-export` serializes the graph\nto JSON; `rendering-auditor` audits a content block's visual output; neither is\n\"render the graph's asset nodes into the site's stylesheets\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What to do, and what not to do",
      "prov:value": "Authoring the skill is a **design act** — a claim about the platform's capability\nvocabulary, inherited by every dependent instance — so it goes to the owner rather\nthan being decided in passing. Bean `yean` carried the two candidates.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean yean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "What to do, and what not to do",
      "prov:value": "**Settled 2026-09-20:** [`site-presentation-assets`](../../ui/theming/site-presentation-assets.md)\nwas authored, and `themes-css` / `avatars-css` are in the graph satisfying it. The\nresolution is recorded here because the alternative — leaving the gap notice\nstanding — is worse than never having written one: an agent that believes a stale\ngap either avoids the capability or rebuilds it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The fourth case: a mechanism with no command, reachable in-process only",
      "prov:value": "Met on 2026-09-20 (bean `0bzg`). `checkFolioProfile` in\n`pipeline/profile-check.ts` catches what schema validation **structurally\ncannot** — a block valid against its own schema but wrong for the folio's content\nprofile, because adapters partition disjointly while profiles nest. Its only caller\nregistered MCP tools. So the check was reachable by an MCP-connected agent and by\n**nothing else**: not a gate, not a sweep, not a person at a shell.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0bzg",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Giving a library function its first command",
      "prov:value": "And the first version of that axis reported **`pass` on a folio that declares no\ncontent type at all** — the laundering it exists to prevent. It guarded on\n`ProfileCheckResult.profile === undefined`, and that field is *never* `undefined`:\n`checkFolioProfile` resolves through `readFolioProfile`, which turns an undeclared\nprofile into `\"paper\"`. That default is **correct for a validator** — the wider\nvocabulary is the safe thing to validate against — and wrong for a reporter, which\nneeds `readDeclaredFolioProfile` instead."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reachability is PLURAL — \"which caller should this have?\" presumes one",
      "prov:value": "**The owner has stated this twice, in the same words both times.** Asked to choose\nbetween three ways of reaching a mechanism: *\"1 2 3 are all triggers\"*, then *\"all\nfor triggers or tools as appropriate\"*. And a day earlier, asked which of three\nmechanisms should start a CI watcher: *\"kick off if like task or workflow initation\nor bean roast\"*. Both times the offered choice was refused, and both times the\nanswer was the same: **one mechanism, several dispatch points.**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Enumerating the dispatch points is also how you find the ones already built",
      "prov:value": "The value is not only completeness. Worked on `translation-roundtrip.ts`\n(bean `vo9d`), where three dispatch points were proposed and, on reading the\nmechanism, **two of the three were already done or wrong**:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean vo9d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The same failure one level out: a KIND, not a mechanism",
      "prov:value": "Cases 1–4 ask what a mechanism is missing. Ask it of a **kind of node** and you\nget the case that cost the owner's time rather than an agent's: an agent counted\n`kg-qa` sidecars over the bean store, found zero, and reported beans\n\"effectively unaudited\". Eight gates audit them."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/covered-is-not-reachable.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this is its own skill",
      "prov:value": "It was written into [`skills-and-tools`](skills-and-tools.md) first, which took\nthat skill from 337 lines to 407 and turned its own `skill-is-brief` criterion\nfrom a pass into a fail — *\"At this length it is a document.\"* The audit was\nright, and the remedy for a skill that has grown a second subject is to split it,\nnot to quiet the finding. Same move as the three-way split of `todo-manager`."
    }
  ]
}
